    "created_at": "2019-07-19T04:49:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-19T04:49:33Z",
    "body": "Rather than create an entirely new `console` function, why not follow a similar route as [`function.displayName`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Function/displayName) and create a `Error.prototype.set displayStack` or `Error.prototype.set customStack` (like [`Error.prototype.stack`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Error/stack)) that the engine can then decide to use in leu of (or in addition to) the actual JavaScript stack?\r\n\r\nFor what it's worth, Web Inspector tries to [detect when a logged string looks like a stack trace, and presents it as such in the UI](https://webkit.org/b/149790).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
